The core question for this morning is whether the "sidecar-level profit-taking"
hypothesis is confirmed or denied by today's closing data.

Both semiconductor majors (005930/000660) are showing positive vs. open,
confirming buyer recovery, and structural catalysts (HBM4E 12-stack,
share buyback) were announced within days. Cost returns of +103% and +182%
respectively mean there is no meaningful basis for adding, and equally,
a single intraday plunge is not sufficient grounds for profit-taking.

The position requiring the most urgent decision is KODEX AI Power Core Infra (487240):
- Cost return -18.2%, 20d -31.6%; the weakness trend is extending,
- No single negative catalyst found, but "profit-taking cycle" coverage persists.
- Deferring add/stop-loss decisions to today's close is possible, but if
  there is an additional -5% decline in subsequent sessions without a trend
  reversal signal, stop-loss and add-buy levels must be pre-defined.

The recommended follow-up: update this report with the 14:00 sidecar status
and 15:30 closing data, plus confirmed foreign flow data.
